    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1975-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Working outward, \\[ \\begin{aligned} 2-\\frac12&=\\frac32,\\\\ 2-\\frac1{\\frac{3}{2}}&=\\frac43,\\\\ 2-\\frac1{\\frac{4}{3}}&=\\frac54. \\end{aligned} \\] The given value is therefore \\(\\frac{1}{\\frac{5}{4}}=\\frac{4}{5}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Evaluate the nested denominator from the inside outward",
        "The three successive inner values are \\(\\frac32,\\frac43,\\) and \\(\\frac54\\)"
      ],
